craft-keymap, craft-menu: the menu bar's shortcut column in the app's words

UNCOMPILED. Written without cargo (not installed where it was written); a later session must run
`cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy -p craft-keymap -p craft-menu --all-targets -- -D warnings`,
`cargo clippy -p craft-keymap --all-targets --features ui -- -D warnings`,
`cargo test -p craft-keymap --features ui` and `cargo test -p craft-menu` before anything is trusted.
Note: no craft-libs workflow runs `cargo test -p craft-menu` (there is no menu.yml); run it by hand.

Base: storytold/craft-libs main 1a11a4897865f7410c40d25ca6e452ce399a1a2c (crates/keymap and
crates/menu are identical at e11f9d9, the rev PdfCraft pins, so it applies there too).
Apply: git apply --check craft-libs-menu-keys.patch && git apply craft-libs-menu-keys.patch

What it does
- craft-keymap: `KeyWord` (Ctrl, Alt, Shift or the key) and `Chord::display_with(platform, &names)`
  / `Trigger::display_with`: `display` with each word named by the app (German Strg+Umschalt+Entf);
  `None` keeps the English word, Mac glyphs are never asked. `display` and `display_for` go
  through the same code with no names, so their output is unchanged.
- craft-keymap (feature `ui`): `I18nText::key_word`, the catalog's `key` rows that `Text::key`
  already reads for the Keyboard Shortcuts dialog, so craft-i18n apps name keys the same way in
  the dialog and in the menus. `Text::key` for `I18nText` now calls it (same lookup).
- craft-menu: `MenuBarUi::key_names(&names)`; the bar writes the shortcut column (and the AccessKit
  keyboard_shortcut, which is the same string) with `display_with`. Without the hook the column
  is exactly as before (`english_key_names` returns None for every word).
- Tests: keymap tests/chord.rs `display_with_names_the_words_and_keeps_the_glyphs`;
  keymap ui/text.rs `key_words_come_from_the_catalogs_key_rows`; menu tests/bar.rs
  `the_shortcut_column_takes_the_apps_key_names`. Revert check: change the bar back to
  `c.display(self.platform)` (bar/mod.rs) and the bar test fails on "Ctrl+Shift+S" != "Strg+Umschalt+S".

